course: dictionary
lesson: 10967
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. A wand is usually a thin stick. «A kitten should play with a wand toy, not your fingers.» Here a wand toy is a toy for play, not a magic stick, because it is for a kitten to play with.
explain: Think about where the word is. In a fairy story, «she waved her wand» means a magic stick. At an airport, a security officer may run a wand over you to check for metal. The word is the same, but the places tell you the meaning.
explain: Look for clue words. «Wand toys with feathers are safer for play with a grown-up.» Feathers and play point to a toy, not a spell. Swap your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have probably got it.
explain: Be careful with phrases too. «There is no magic wand» does not mean you cannot find a magic stick. It means there is no quick, easy solution to a problem.
fact: A wand is a thin stick used by a magician, wizard or fairy to do magic or spells.
fact: A wand can also be any thin rod or stick-shaped tool, such as a mascara wand or a metal-detector wand.
fact: In real life a magician's wand has no real power; the magic comes from skill and misdirection.
fact: «Wave a wand» and «magic wand» are phrases to remember.
fact: «There is no magic wand» means there is no quick, easy solution.
exercise: «A kitten should play with a wand toy, not your fingers.» What is a wand toy here? | A tiny fairy | A real magic stick that casts spells | A metal bar for finding coins | *A toy on a stick for play
exercise: At an airport, a security officer runs a wand over your coat. What is the wand for? | *To check for metal | To make you invisible | To cast a spell on your bag | To write your name on the coat
exercise: «There is no magic wand for this maths problem.» What does this phrase mean? | You must wave a wand to solve it | *There is no quick, easy solution | The problem is magic and cannot be solved | The teacher has a secret wand
test: Which phrase means there is no quick, easy solution? | Magic wand toy | *There is no magic wand | Thin rod with feathers | Wave a wand
test: In real life, does a magician's wand have real power? | *No, the magic comes from skill and misdirection | Yes, but only on Tuesdays | Yes, the wand always works | No, because wands are made of plastic
exam: Which of these is a wand that is not used for magic? | A wizard's wand in a film | A fairy godmother's wand | *A mascara wand | A magician's wand on stage
